  {"date": "2021-08-06", "venue": "Ruoff Music Center", "city": "Noblesville", "state": "IN", "gap": 4, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "The actual \"Sand\" proper is taken at a slower and milkshake-thick pace, and the band luxuriates in the usual \"Sand\" jam until about the 7:30 mark, when Trey hits on a particularly gorgeous major-key riff and the band follows him to a very pretty space. Page's work on the keys and Mike's rock-steady accompaniment are what to look out for here. Pretty strong peak at the end, too.", "prev": "Wolfman's Brother", "next": "Lawn Boy", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2021-08-13", "venue": "Atlantic City Beach", "city": "Atlantic City", "state": "NJ", "gap": 5, "set": "1", "prev": "Rift", "xnext": "Tweezer", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2021-08-28", "venue": "Gorge Amphitheatre", "city": "George", "state": "WA", "gap": 4, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "The jam begins typically with solid, funky playing led by Trey and with Page's crunchy keyboard action. Around 7:00, there is a noticeable break to major mode. The forces seem to gather, suggestive of an oncoming peak. Instead, the band seems to luxuriate in this blissful mode, stretching and exploring the terrain without ever pushing the sentiment over the top. The intensity gradually diminishes, but the warm sentiment continues before devolving to transition space.", "out": ">", "next": "Down with Disease", "xprev": "Say It To Me S.A.N.T.O.S.", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2021-09-05", "venue": "Dick's Sporting Goods Park", "city": "Commerce City", "state": "CO", "gap": 6, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "This isn't your typical \"Sand\" jam, as the start of it wouldn't be out of place at the beginning of a \"Tube\" jam. Things mellow out later, then get to a murky outer-space place. The most impressive thing about this jam is Jon Fishman's refusal to quit; he is fantastic throughout. > a must-hear \"Sigma Oasis.\"", "note": "Unfinished.", "out": ">", "prev": "McGrupp and the Watchful Hosemasters", "next": "Sigma Oasis", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2021-10-15", "venue": "Golden 1 Center", "city": "Sacramento", "state": "CA", "gap": 1, "set": "e", "xprev": "Golgi Apparatus", "last": 1, "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2021-10-23", "venue": "North Island Credit Union Amphitheatre", "city": "Chula Vista", "state": "CA", "gap": 6, "set": "2", "out": "->", "prev": "Joy", "in": ">", "next": "Piper", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2021-10-29", "venue": "MGM Grand Garden Arena", "city": "Las Vegas", "state": "NV", "gap": 4, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Trey wastes no time getting a \"Tweezer\" tease in, kicking off a \"blissy\" jam. No longer chained to the song's bass line, Mike has some very inventive play. The \"bliss\" gives way to Trey going heavy on his effects, and eventually -> \"Tweezer.\"", "out": "->", "prev": "Reba", "next": "Tweezer", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2022-02-24", "venue": "Moon Palace", "city": "Cancun", "state": "Quintana Roo", "gap": 4, "set": "1", "prev": "Sigma Oasis", "xnext": "So Damn Lucky", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2022-04-22", "venue": "Madison Square Garden", "city": "New York", "state": "NY", "gap": 6, "set": "3", "jamchart": true, "jam": "An extremely efficient jam that concisely hits on a lot of sweet mini-movements beginning with a bubbly major groove at 4:20. Later returns to minor tonality with an edge and Trey finds a nice descending theme.", "prev": "Waves", "in": ">", "next": "Split Open and Melt", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2022-05-27", "venue": "The Wharf Amphitheater", "city": "Orange Beach", "state": "AL", "gap": 2, "set": "1", "prev": "Halley's Comet", "in": ">", "next": "The Old Home Place", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2022-06-05", "venue": "Ruoff Music Center", "city": "Noblesville", "state": "IN", "gap": 7, "set": "2", "times": 2, "jamchart": true, "jam": "Breaks away at 7:00 and never looks back, blending multiple bliss sections with darker-tinged synth/delay play (including a \"Crosseyed\" tease from Mike at 12:00) all within the first twenty minutes. Shortly before 22:00 a tidal wave of sound starts building as the jam crests in a series of massive peaks, after which a final easy-going segment serves as an effective exhale.", "next": "Sigma Oasis", "xprev": "The Moma Dance", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2022-07-14", "venue": "Xfinity Center", "city": "Mansfield", "state": "MA", "gap": 1, "set": "2", "prev": "Bug", "in": ">", "xnext": "Punch You in the Eye", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2022-07-24", "venue": "Xfinity Theatre", "city": "Hartford", "state": "CT", "gap": 7, "set": "1", "prev": "Limb By Limb", "xnext": "A Wave of Hope", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2022-07-30", "venue": "Merriweather Post Pavilion", "city": "Columbia", "state": "MD", "gap": 4, "set": "1", "next": "If I Could", "first": 1, "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2022-08-05", "venue": "Atlantic City Beach", "city": "Atlantic City", "state": "NJ", "gap": 4, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "After a brief passage of standard \"Sand\" fare, the music modulates at 5:15 for major key. The band\nimmediately locks onto an anthemic chord progression, with Page's grand piano bed providing a solid\nplatform for Trey's soaring guitar. The main \"Sand\" riff reappears at the 10 minute mark, as the tune\npatiently winds down. > \"Plasma.\"", "out": ">", "prev": "Wilson", "in": ">", "next": "Plasma", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2022-08-10", "venue": "Budweiser Stage", "city": "Toronto", "state": "Ontario", "gap": 3, "set": "1", "prev": "Stash", "xnext": "Sample in a Jar", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2022-09-01", "venue": "Dick's Sporting Goods Park", "city": "Commerce City", "state": "CO", "gap": 4, "set": "1", "note": "Unfinished.", "out": "->", "next": "Down with Disease", "first": 1, "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2022-12-30", "venue": "Madison Square Garden", "city": "New York", "state": "NY", "gap": 6, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Flirts with a few blissful passages in the first half, but at 10:45 this version locks into a propulsive, heavy jam with Trey pouring on a bevy of punishing riffs, and then wraps up with a final cimb interspersed in the traditional closing.", "out": ">", "prev": "Golden Age", "next": "If I Could", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2023-02-23", "venue": "Moon Palace", "city": "Cancun", "state": "Quintana Roo", "gap": 2, "set": "1", "out": ">", "prev": "My Friend, My Friend", "next": "Sample in a Jar", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2023-04-17", "venue": "William Randolph Hearst Greek Theatre, University of California, Berkeley ", "city": "Berkeley", "state": "CA", "gap": 6, "set": "e", "prev": "Miss You", "last": 1, "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2023-07-16", "venue": "Ameris Bank Amphitheatre", "city": "Alpharetta", "state": "GA", "gap": 10, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "The band eschews the typical \"Sand\" guitar-led jam for immediate introspective exploration. The music grows inward, with Trey's thoughtfully psychedelic approach leading the way. Page's enveloping synth and electric piano textures spread the music out, while Fish and Mike provide an indefatigable, dynamic pulse. The music eventually returns to the \"Sand\" riff to close, and > \"Reba\".", "out": ">", "prev": "Weekapaug Groove", "next": "Reba", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2023-07-22", "venue": "The Pavilion at Star Lake", "city": "Burgettstown", "state": "PA", "gap": 4, "set": "1", "prev": "Ass Handed", "xnext": "Everything's Right", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2023-08-04", "venue": "Madison Square Garden", "city": "New York", "state": "NY", "gap": 9, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Acting as the palate cleanser between a titanic \"Mike's Song\" and a breakneck \"Crosseyed and Painless\", this version opts for supreme patience despite its short run-time. Trey's throwback Whammy loops\nset the tone, as the band settles into a blissy psychedelic space. This then slowly builds to a swirl of hose-y playing before setting MSG on fire with a -> \"Crosseyed\".", "out": "->", "prev": "Mike's Song", "in": ">", "next": "Crosseyed and Painless", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2023-08-25", "venue": "Broadview Stage at SPAC", "city": "Saratoga Springs", "state": "NY", "gap": 2, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "The \"We Welcome You to Munchkinland\" teases from Trey start at 6:45 and don't stop as they become the theme of this bizarrely triumphant jam on the 84th Anniversary of \"The Wizard of Oz's\" release.", "prev": "Punch You in the Eye", "next": "Rock and Roll", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2023-09-01", "venue": "Dick's Sporting Goods Park", "city": "Commerce City", "state": "CO", "gap": 3, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Another year at Dick's produces yet another monster version of \"Sand.\" Strong play from Mike and Page kicks this jam off in fun fashion. Ideas are thrown out from each band member, with nothing ever sticking for too long. If a portion of this jam doesn't hook you, just give it two minutes and the next section will. Trey finds some lilting riffs towards the end, and then the whole band locks into a rocking, fun jam before meandering back to the familiar territory of the song proper, briefly jamming the outro. > \"NMINML\".", "out": ">", "next": "No Men In No Man's Land", "xprev": "David Bowie", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2023-10-07", "venue": "Bridgestone Arena", "city": "Nashville", "state": "TN", "gap": 4, "set": "2", "out": ">", "prev": "Life Saving Gun", "in": "->", "next": "Everything's Right", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2023-10-13", "venue": "United Center", "city": "Chicago", "state": "IL", "gap": 4, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "A fantastic sort of throwback to \"Sands\" of the late 1.0 era in that it doesn't range far from the format, but in doing so is able to drill down into the entrancing groove even deeper with loops and synths aplenty over top of a rock-solid rhythm section. Around 9:30, the reins are loosened slightly, allowing the jam to transition to major and Page to really show out for a spell, but the ominous minor tone soon returns to see things through to the conclusion.", "next": "Waves", "xprev": "Drift While You're Sleeping", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2023-12-29", "venue": "Madison Square Garden", "city": "New York", "state": "NY", "gap": 4, "set": "2", "prev": "My Friend, My Friend", "in": "->", "next": "About to Run", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2024-02-21", "venue": "Moon Palace", "city": "Cancun", "state": "Quintana Roo", "gap": 3, "set": "1", "out": ">", "prev": "Julius", "next": "Life Saving Gun", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2024-04-18", "venue": "Sphere", "city": "Las Vegas", "state": "NV", "gap": 4, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Spends little time in the typical \"Sand\" zone with an early modulation to major and is soon transformed into a dreamy soundscape awash with synths. Over the next several minutes, the jam is gradually shaped by subtly shifting riffs while maintaining its ethereal heading, until a more grounded peaking section emerges in the final minutes.", "out": ">", "next": "Tweezer", "xprev": "Carini", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2024-07-20", "venue": "Xfinity Center", "city": "Mansfield", "state": "MA", "gap": 5, "set": "1", "out": ">", "prev": "Back on the Train", "next": "Bouncing Around the Room", "nb": 1},
