  {"date": "2024-08-15", "venue": "The Woodlands", "city": "Dover", "state": "DE", "gap": 2, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Strong set-closer marked by impressive, collective, improvisation. Patient, Trey pushes the band to, and through, a pointed peak before the band returns to land \"Sand's\" signature riff.", "prev": "A Wave of Hope", "xnext": "What's Going Through Your Mind", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2024-08-30", "venue": "Dick's Sporting Goods Park", "city": "Commerce City", "state": "CO", "gap": 5, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Less Sand (although, astonishingly, the band keeps the song's signature line - mostly - running throughout) and more method of critical analysis of philosophical and musical language, one which emphasizes the internal workings of expression and conceptual systems, the relational quality of meaning, and the assumptions implicit in Phish-forms of expression. > \"Ruby Waves\".", "prev": "Chalk Dust Torture", "next": "Ruby Waves", "nb": 1},
